// Runa, capercaillie, Kettil's daughter (character-bibles.md §3). Her image: counting people, sung.
// Voice: warm, loud, sings mid-sentence; "we" for her town even alone; never "I don't know how".
// The bell (Bell_2): the nightly roll-call. She counts Wren in once as "stranger, one" and never again calls her
// stranger. The lesson walk (bounds-walk.md, Kettil's Rest) is taught here.

title: Bell_Runa_Count
---
<<if has_flag("emberdown.runa.counted")>>
    <<jump Bell_Runa_Named>>
<<endif>>
<<sing runa>>
Runa: Thirty-nine. Forty. Forty-one. Hold on. #face:bright #line:02ffce4
Runa: Forty-two, stranger, one. Stand where I can count you. #face:bright #line:087f6ba
-> I'm not staying. #line:0bd3f62
    <<voice warden emberdown>>
    Runa: Nobody's staying. We're counted anyway. That's the whole trick of it. #face:bright #line:096d840
-> Who taught you the song? #line:0530008
    <<voice surveyor emberdown>>
    Runa: Mother. Before the smoke. She says the mine taught her. We don't ask the mine. #face:grave #line:0c3c636
-> ... #line:087376e
    <<voice drift emberdown>>
    Runa: Quiet ones count too. Louder, next time. We'll learn you. #face:bright #line:089c28d
<<flag emberdown.runa.counted 1>>
Runa: The walk goes round the town on the beat. Every street a name, every name a step. #face:bright #line:058b207
Runa: Miss three and we start the verse again. Nobody's ever lost for missing. That's the kindness in it. #face:bright #line:049c2f2
-> Teach me. #line:03f591d
    <<voice surveyor emberdown>>
    Runa: Stand on the well-cap when I sing "well". We'll learn the rest walking. #face:bright #line:0df17f0
    <<flag holdfast.walk_learned 1>>
    <<walk kettils_rest>>
-> Another night. #line:08ac58f
    <<voice drift emberdown>>
    Runa: Every night's another night. That's what the bell is for. #face:bright #line:023359f
===

title: Bell_Runa_Named
---
<<if has_flag("emberdown.hollowvein.walked") or walked("Saltmarrow_B")>>
    <<if not has_flag("runa.named_wren")>>
        Runa: Forty-two, Wren. She's not always here. Doesn't matter. That's the point. #face:bright #line:0a23e38
        Runa: You held a place by walking it. Now we hold you the same way. Every night, your name. #face:bright #line:0ab2143
        Runa: Take the count with you. Mother's rule: everyone in it, and you in it too. #face:bright #line:0ed29dc
        Runa: Forty-two, Wren. Sing it back wherever you are. That's a place held. #face:bright #line:0934c10
        <<bind kettil.count>>
        <<flag runa.named_wren 1>>
    <<else>>
        Runa: Forty-two, Wren. Forty-three, whoever's next. We're counting up again. First time in years. #still #face:bright #line:0f9d542
    <<endif>>
<<else>>
    Runa: Forty-two, and you. The count's warmer with you in it. #still #face:bright #line:0fa9c4e
    <<if not walk_known()>>
        Runa: The walk's still waiting for you. Stand on the well-cap when I sing "well". #face:bright #line:04c6759
        <<flag holdfast.walk_learned 1>>
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
// Act 2: a fish village with nine songs and nobody counting them. Asked, she comes to the coast (Merrow_Runa).
<<if has_flag("act2.started") and has_flag("saltmarrow.dotha.songs") and not walked("Saltmarrow_B") and flag("saltmarrow.dotha.decided") != 2 and not has_flag("emberdown.runa.asked_for_merrow")>>
    Runa: You've a look. Somebody somewhere isn't counted. Say it. #still #face:asking #line:08b9a13
    -> Merrow's End. Nine songs, nobody counting. #line:0d499a6
        <<voice surveyor emberdown>>
        Runa: A fish village. Nobody's counted a fish village. We'll walk it. After the bell; the bell comes first. #face:bright #line:04cf0e9
        <<flag emberdown.runa.asked_for_merrow 1>>
    -> Come to the coast and see it. #line:04287ec
        <<voice warden emberdown>>
        Runa: Show me? I'll be singing it before you've finished pointing. After the bell. #face:bright #line:0bf8a27
        <<flag emberdown.runa.asked_for_merrow 1>>
    -> ... #line:084196a
        <<voice drift emberdown>>
        Runa: Keep it, then. The count keeps too. Ask when you're ready. #still #line:0e92cdb
<<endif>>
===
